    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d295-a3">

                <pb facs="0495" n="399" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg399"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Augur to Colonel Shafter.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Headquarters Department of Texas, Office of Assistant
                                Adjutant-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San Antonio,
                                Texas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1872-02-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 2, 1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 25th ultimo, respecting the body of Mexicans that crossed
                    into this country, in pursuit of Indians, and asking instructions in such cases.
                    In reply, the commanding general directs me to say that you will pursue and
                    capture, if possible, any armed body of Mexicans that come into our territory.
                    Should you succeed in capturing any, hold them prisoners, and report the facts
                    to these headquarters.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>J. A. AUGUR,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Assistant
                                    Adjutant-General.</hi></item>
                            <item>Lieutenant-Colonel <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. R.
                                    Shafter</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Twenty-fourth
                                    Infantry, commanding Fort Davis. Texas.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
